# Stage handoff. The pipeline stages leave files here for the next one — the
# request, both plans, the commits patch, the validation report, the assembled
# PR body. It is scratch, never part of a change: nothing in it may ever be
# committed. This entry is the first line of that defence (a `git add -A`
# cannot pick up an ignored path); ci-validate.sh is the second, and fails any
# commit that touches .ci-handoff/ anyway, because `git add -f` exists.
.ci-handoff/

# Test scratch
/tmp/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local agent permission rules — MUST stay untracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Bun (the rewrite lands here)
node_modules/
